# Every text file is LF in the repository *and* in the working tree.
#
# Why this exists: with no attributes and `core.autocrlf=false`, nothing kept the
# two in step. 368 tracked files were LF in the index and CRLF on disk, and 26
# were mixed, while `git status` reported the tree clean — so the difference was
# invisible until some tool rewrote a file and preserved its CRLF, at which point
# a three-line change surfaced as a seven-hundred-line diff. That happened
# repeatedly and was worked around per file; this is the cause.
#
# `eol=lf` is the half that matters: `text=auto` alone normalizes the index and
# leaves the working tree to the platform, which is exactly the split that hid
# this.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
